kelly fitzgibbons was one of 118 women  killed by a man over the course of 12  months in the uk  she was shot dead by her partner who  also killed their two little girls ava  who was four  and lexi who was two their three lives  were erased in a matter of seconds  i met kelly and her twin sister emma at  the youth club just there when we were  all 13.  sue redmond was kelly's best friend and  often comes to this memorial bench where  they first met as school girls  in bosom in west sussex to think about  her  it's so important purely because it's  it's raised our awareness  we had no idea until someone gave us the  heads up that  kelly's name had been read out in the  house of commons we had absolutely no  idea of the number of women  i i wouldn't even have thought there  were that many murders in the uk per  year let alone  women murdered at the hands of men it's  just truly shocking and  and it's very very right what just  phillips has done  in this place on international women's  day labor mp jess phillips read out in  parliament the names of  all the women killed by men over the  course of a year  in britain kelly fitzgibbons killed  alongside her two daughters  artist tenny beaumont saw that speech  and decided to paint a portrait  of every single woman i was obviously  hugely saddened but i was also really  shocked that actually the only name  i recognized at that point was sarah  everard  and actually she wasn't on the list yet  but she did mention her name  and it just made me think you know it  made me  curious in a way about who all these  other women were and why we didn't know  them  kelly's twin sister has set up a  charitable foundation in her name  to provide support and legal advice to  families  whose loved ones die in traumatic  circumstances  henny says the aim of her work is to  remember  honor and make all these women visible  ender brady sky news
 

